ve). Preference pairs constructed with the same criterion: which response better advances cooperative success.\n- A3 \u2014 Guess-My-City: same constraints; descriptive/cooperative game, neutral critic feedback.\n- C1 \u2014 No-training control (base model, same checkpoints/decoding).\n- C2 \u2014 Imitation-only control: teacher-generated preference data with NO self-play episodes (single-pass supervised/DPO data from the teacher), matched in pair count to the game arms. This separates imitation learning from self-play effects.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3. CONTROLLED VARIABLES AND CONFOUND PREVENTION (explicit controls)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nConfounds and their controls:\n(a) Teacher/critic quality \u2192 SAME fixed judge/critic model in all arms (default: a fixed strong open-weights model at a frozen checkpoint; GPT-4 variant see \u00a77). The critic prompt differs only in the adversarial instruction; an identical system prompt skeleton is used. Critic identity and temperature are logged and frozen.\n(b) Data volume \u2192 Matched budgets: identical number of generated episodes, extracted preference pairs, and optimizer updates across A1\u2013A3 and C2. If one game yields fewer valid pairs per episode, keep training pairs matched by generating more episodes only up to the fixed episode cap and record the shortfall \u2014 do not silently top up.\n(c) Training hyperparameters \u2192 identical optimizer, learning rate, batch size, and schedule; one shared pilot sweep on A1, then frozen for all arms (avoids per-arm tuning bias).\n(d) Prompt/format leakage \u2192 no game-format text in evaluation prompts; evaluation prompts are benchmark-native.\n(e) Rater bias \u2192 all free-text judging automated with the same fixed judge; judge never sees the arm label; spot-check a sample with human raters for judge-drift.\n(f) Selection bias in episodes \u2192 games drawn from a shared entity/word pool split into disjoint train/held-out sets; no entity appears in both.\n(g) Seed variance \u2192 \u22653 independent training seeds per arm (A1\u2013A3, C2), same seeds across arms for paired comparison.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n4. MODELS AND EVALUATION\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nBase models (ASSUMPTION \u2014 recollection of SPAG, unverified): LLaMA-2-7B-Chat and LLaMA-3-8B-Instruct; if resource-constrained, run the primary model first (Llama-3-8B-Instruct) and add the second only in the extended budget. One model is sufficient for the primary claim; the second tests generality.\n\nEvaluation, per fixed decision (1):\n- PRIMARY: transfer to held-out standard reasoning benchmarks. Proposed suite (ASSUMPTION \u2014 unverified list; substitute the paper's suite if topics provide it): 3\u20134 benchmarks spanning distinct reasoning types, e.g., BBH (multi-task reasoning), GSM8K (math), ARC-Challenge (science reasoning), MMLU (knowledge/reasoning). Held-out splits only; no benchmark data used anywhere in training. Decoding and prompting templates frozen across arms.\n- SECONDARY: in-game held-out performance \u2014 win/success rate on held-out game instances for each arm's own game, plus a cross-game probe (A1's model evaluated on A2/A3 games) to measure generality of the trained behavior.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n5. SELF-PLAY BUDGET AND CONFIGURATIONS (per fixed decision (2))\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nIteration structure: R rounds of (episode generation \u2192 critic labeling \u2192 preference-pair extraction \u2192 DPO-style training), identical R for all arms.\n\nPRIMARY (feasible at paper-like scale, ASSUMPTION on scale):\n- R = 2 rounds; ~2,000 episodes per round per arm; target \u22652,000 preference pairs per arm; ~1,000 optimizer updates total.\n- Seeds: 3 per arm. Arms trained: A1, A2, A3, C2 (4 arms \u00d7 3 seeds = 12 training runs) + 2 base models evaluated (no training).\n- Cost driver: critic/teacher labeling (\u22488k+ episode judgments). Estimate ~O(10\u2077) teacher tokens per arm.\n\nREDUCED-BUDGET VARIANT:\n- 1 base model (Llama-3-8B-Instruct only), R = 1 round, ~800 episodes/arm, \u2265800 pairs/arm, 3 seeds for A1\u2013A3 but 1 seed for C2 (its role is directional, not the headline test).\n- Sensitivity note: with R=1 and fewer pairs, absolute gains shrink and CIs widen; conclusions should be reported as \"direction of effect with CI\" not significance-claimed if power is low. A pre-registered minimum detectable effect (e.g., \u22652 points benchmark accuracy) should be stated; if the reduced budget's power falls below detecting that MDE, the reduced variant supports only qualitative ordering.\n\nBudget sensitivity statement: because the true budget is unknown, the design is robust in structure (matched budgets, same controls) at any scale; what degrades with budget is statistical power and the second-model generality check, not the internal validity of the comparison.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n6. ANALYSIS PLAN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n- Per arm and seed: \u0394benchmark = mean held-out benchmark accuracy(post \u2212 pre). Primary contrast: \u0394(A1) \u2212 max/mean of \u0394(A2), \u0394(A3); report per benchmark and pooled.\n- Statistics: paired comparisons across matched seeds; bootstrap CIs (10k resamples over benchmark items) plus a seed-level paired permutation test. Alpha = 0.05, Holm correction across the primary contrasts (A1 vs A2, A1 vs A3).\n- Also report effect sizes and CIs (not just p-values), and per-seed spread to expose self-play variance.\n- H3 check: \u0394(C2) vs \u0394(A1..A3) with the same procedure.\n- Pre-registration of the primary endpoint (pooled benchmark delta) before any training run to prevent benchmark-shopping.\n- Failure modes to report explicitly: invalid episode yield per game, preference-pair shortfall, critic rejection rates \u2014 these are evidence about whether games are comparably trainable, part of the answer, not noise to hide.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. JUDGE/CRITIC CONFIGURATION (per fixed decision (3))\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n- CONTROLLED DEFAULT: a single fixed open-weights strong model (frozen checkpoint) as critic and imitation target in every arm, including C2. Rationale: removes API-cost uncertainty and guarantees identical teacher across arms; limitation: weaker teacher may cap imitation quality identically in all arms (does not bias the contrast).\n- ALTERNATIVE (paper-faithful variant): GPT-4 as critic in all arms, if access exists. Same matched-budget controls apply. If both are run, this becomes a teacher-strength factor in a 2\u00d73 sub-design.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n8. FEASIBILITY AND DESIGN-ONLY STATUS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nFeasibility (if ever executed): 12 fine-tuning runs of \u22648B models are modest; the binding constraint is teacher labeling volume, mitigated by the fixed-critic default. The current environment (network disabled, no GPU, no ML packages) could not execute any part of this \u2014 as required, this is a design only.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\